Subject: [PATCH] Add FLAG_P700_INIT to the PT-P710BT device entry

Without the P700-family init sequence the PT-P710BT accepts the raster job
over USB (ptouch-print exits 0) but never prints: the printer drops into an
error state (status error = 0x0100, "replace media" bit) and flashes its LED
red until power-cycled. The PT-P710BT uses the same print engine as the
PT-P700/PT-P750W, which both carry FLAG_P700_INIT.

Verified on a PT-P710BT (USB ID 04f9:20af, 24mm TZe tape): with this flag the
same jobs print correctly and the status stays error = 0x0000.
---
--- a/src/libptouch.c
+++ b/src/libptouch.c
@@ -97,7 +97,7 @@
 	   Brother "Software Developer's Manual - Raster Command Reference,
 	   PT-P900/P900W/P950NW", section 2.3.5 "Raster line". */
-	{0x04f9, 0x20af, "PT-P710BT", 128, 180, FLAG_RASTER_PACKBITS|FLAG_HAS_PRECUT, 0},
+	{0x04f9, 0x20af, "PT-P710BT", 128, 180, FLAG_RASTER_PACKBITS|FLAG_P700_INIT|FLAG_HAS_PRECUT, 0},
 	{0x04f9, 0x20df, "PT-D410", 128, 180, FLAG_USE_INFO_CMD|FLAG_HAS_PRECUT|FLAG_D460BT_MAGIC, 0},
 	{0x04f9, 0x20e0, "PT-D460BT", 128, 180, FLAG_P700_INIT|FLAG_USE_INFO_CMD|FLAG_HAS_PRECUT|FLAG_D460BT_MAGIC, 0},
